1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,832
Twenty-ninth of May, 2024. Athens.

2
00:00:05,962 --> 00:00:11,988
The final of the Europa Conference League,
Olympiacos against Fiorentina.

3
00:00:12,118 --> 00:00:18,071
Ninety minutes have gone. Nobody has
scored, and in the stands, nobody can sit

4
00:00:18,111 --> 00:00:18,531
down.

5
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:24,827
And here is the strange part. The final is
in Athens, at the Agia

6
00:00:24,867 --> 00:00:28,312
Sophia Stadium. The home of AEK.

7
00:00:28,442 --> 00:00:32,360
A rival's ground, and nine thousand
tickets for each club.

8
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:37,007
No Greek club had ever won a European
trophy.

9
00:00:37,137 --> 00:00:42,727
Only one had even reached a European
final: Panathinaikos, in

10
00:00:42,767 --> 00:00:46,067
1971, and they lost it to Ajax.

11
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:51,157
This is the most successful club in the
history of Greek football.

12
00:00:51,287 --> 00:00:57,140
A hundred years old. And in all those
years,

13
00:00:57,430 --> 00:00:59,633
the furthest they had ever gone in Europe
was a quarter-final of the Champions

14
00:00:59,673 --> 00:01:02,630
League, in 1999.

15
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:08,429
Thirteen days before this final,
Olympiacos had turned a hundred.

16
00:01:08,559 --> 00:01:14,436
And now, in the second half of extra time,
the whole of that hundred years is

17
00:01:14,476 --> 00:01:15,194
sitting on one ball.

18
00:01:15,870 --> 00:01:20,461
Hold that moment there. Because to
understand what this night meant to the

19
00:01:20,501 --> 00:01:25,872
people in those stands, we have to go back
to August 2023, to

20
00:01:25,912 --> 00:01:29,756
Piraeus, and a season that very nearly
fell apart.

21
00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:37,130
The season began in the Europa League,
with a new manager, Diego Martínez,

22
00:01:37,350 --> 00:01:41,239
appointed in June, and two qualifying
rounds to get through.

23
00:01:41,950 --> 00:01:47,980
Genk first. One-nil in Piraeus, Kostas
Fortounis in the first minute.

24
00:01:48,110 --> 00:01:54,001
Then Belgium, one-all, and Sotiris
Alexandropoulos in the ninetieth

25
00:01:54,041 --> 00:01:54,908
minute to see it through.

26
00:01:55,590 --> 00:01:59,830
Then Čukarički of Belgrade, three-one and
three-nil.

27
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:05,503
And the group: Freiburg, West Ham, and
TSC, from a small Serbian town called

28
00:02:05,543 --> 00:02:08,908
Bačka Topola. Remember that name.

29
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:12,893
West Ham came to Piraeus in October.

30
00:02:13,023 --> 00:02:17,704
Two-one. Fortounis, and Rodinei just
before half-time.

31
00:02:17,834 --> 00:02:19,939
A night to tell people about.

32
00:02:20,630 --> 00:02:24,363
Freiburg in Piraeus, in September:
two-three.

33
00:02:24,493 --> 00:02:28,132
El Kaabi scored twice, and it still was
not enough.

34
00:02:28,262 --> 00:02:32,106
Then West Ham away, one-nil to them, in
November.

35
00:02:32,790 --> 00:02:35,839
Then Freiburg away, at the end of
November.

36
00:02:35,969 --> 00:02:37,143
Five-nil.

37
00:02:37,870 --> 00:02:43,219
The last group game, against TSC at home
in December, finished five-two.

38
00:02:43,349 --> 00:02:48,054
It changed nothing. Third place had been
settled already.

39
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:53,011
Seven points from six games. Third in the
group.

40
00:02:53,141 --> 00:02:58,479
Not out of Europe, just down a level, into
the knockout play-offs of the Europa

41
00:02:58,519 --> 00:03:01,535
Conference League. The third competition.

42
00:03:02,230 --> 00:03:08,055
Martínez left in December. Carlos
Carvalhal came in, and was gone

43
00:03:08,095 --> 00:03:09,135
by February.

44
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:14,443
Every club has supporters who remember
things no record keeps.

45
00:03:14,573 --> 00:03:19,128
If you're one of them, subscribe, and tell
us your season in the comments.

46
00:03:19,258 --> 00:03:21,935
The best stories come from the terrace.

47
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:29,783
On the eleventh of February, 2024,
Olympiacos appointed

48
00:03:29,823 --> 00:03:35,289
José Luis Mendilibar. The spring before,
he had won the Europa League with

49
00:03:35,329 --> 00:03:36,055
Sevilla.

50
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:41,745
Three managers in one season is not how
trophies are usually won.

51
00:03:41,875 --> 00:03:44,700
This season was going to be different.

52
00:03:44,830 --> 00:03:47,582
Nobody in Piraeus knew it yet.

53
00:03:48,270 --> 00:03:54,320
He had days, not weeks, before a knockout
tie against Ferencváros of Budapest.

54
00:03:55,030 --> 00:03:59,561
One-nil in Piraeus. One-nil in Budapest.

55
00:03:59,691 --> 00:04:04,775
Both goals from the same man, the Moroccan
striker Ayoub El Kaabi.

56
00:04:04,905 --> 00:04:06,867
Remember that name, too.

57
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:12,627
Round of sixteen. Maccabi Tel Aviv.

58
00:04:12,757 --> 00:04:16,723
The first leg in Piraeus, on the seventh
of March.

59
00:04:17,390 --> 00:04:22,971
One-four. At home. El Kaabi scored, and it
hardly mattered.

60
00:04:23,101 --> 00:04:26,802
Three goals behind, with ninety minutes
left to play.

61
00:04:27,510 --> 00:04:31,646
It was a long walk home from the
Karaiskakis that night.

62
00:04:31,776 --> 00:04:35,442
Three goals is a lot to find in a second
leg.

63
00:04:35,572 --> 00:04:37,753
Almost nobody finds them.

64
00:04:38,470 --> 00:04:41,772
The second leg was not played in Tel Aviv.

65
00:04:41,902 --> 00:04:47,409
Maccabi played their home games that
season in Serbia, at the TSC Arena in

66
00:04:47,449 --> 00:04:52,987
Bačka Topola. The same small ground where
Olympiacos had drawn in

67
00:04:53,027 --> 00:04:54,060
October.

68
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:58,435
In the ground that night: three hundred
and seventy people.

69
00:04:58,565 --> 00:05:01,214
Everyone else watched from somewhere else.

70
00:05:01,910 --> 00:05:04,906
Daniel Podence after ten minutes.

71
00:05:05,036 --> 00:05:09,166
Fortounis. El Kaabi, just before
half-time.

72
00:05:09,296 --> 00:05:11,733
Three-nil, and the tie was level.

73
00:05:12,430 --> 00:05:18,541
El Kaabi again. Four-nil. Then a penalty
for Maccabi, and four-one.

74
00:05:18,671 --> 00:05:22,004
Five each on aggregate after ninety
minutes.

75
00:05:22,710 --> 00:05:28,407
Extra time. Stevan Jovetić. Youssef
El-Arabi.

76
00:05:28,537 --> 00:05:33,091
Six-one. From three goals down to seven
goals to five.

77
00:05:33,221 --> 00:05:36,403
Olympiacos were in the quarter-finals.

78
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:41,420
Quarter-final. Fenerbahçe.

79
00:05:42,110 --> 00:05:47,566
Three-two in Piraeus. Fortounis, Jovetić,
Chiquinho.

80
00:05:47,696 --> 00:05:53,098
Three-nil after fifty-seven minutes, and
then two Fenerbahçe goals that made the

81
00:05:53,138 --> 00:05:55,830
trip to Istanbul feel very long.

82
00:05:56,550 --> 00:06:02,123
The eighteenth of April. The Şükrü
Saracoğlu, and 44,040

83
00:06:02,163 --> 00:06:03,600
people.

84
00:06:04,270 --> 00:06:07,724
İrfan Can Kahveci in the twelfth minute.

85
00:06:07,854 --> 00:06:13,258
Three each on aggregate. Then extra time,
and nobody else scored.

86
00:06:13,990 --> 00:06:20,121
Penalties. And in goal for Olympiacos,
Konstantinos Tzolakis.

87
00:06:20,790 --> 00:06:25,745
Dušan Tadić. Saved. Cengiz Ünder.

88
00:06:25,875 --> 00:06:30,197
Saved. Leonardo Bonucci. Saved.

89
00:06:30,327 --> 00:06:32,954
Three penalties, in Istanbul.

90
00:06:33,670 --> 00:06:39,470
Three-two on penalties. For the first time
in their history, Olympiacos were in

91
00:06:39,510 --> 00:06:41,613
a European semi-final.

92
00:06:42,310 --> 00:06:47,233
When the team flew home, the supporters
were waiting for them at the airport to

93
00:06:47,273 --> 00:06:52,123
welcome back a team that had just done
something no Olympiacos side had ever

94
00:06:52,163 --> 00:06:52,567
done.

95
00:06:54,620 --> 00:07:00,454
A few days later, in Nyon, in Switzerland,
the

96
00:07:00,494 --> 00:07:03,619
Olympiacos youth team beat Milan three-nil
in the final of the UEFA Youth

97
00:07:03,659 --> 00:07:08,496
League. The first Greek team ever to win a
UEFA club competition.

98
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:14,802
Semi-final. Aston Villa. The first leg in
Birmingham, on the

99
00:07:14,842 --> 00:07:15,806
second of May.

100
00:07:16,510 --> 00:07:19,076
El Kaabi in the sixteenth minute.

101
00:07:19,206 --> 00:07:22,337
The twenty-ninth. The fifty-sixth.

102
00:07:22,467 --> 00:07:26,817
A hat-trick in England, and Santiago Hezze
for the fourth.

103
00:07:26,947 --> 00:07:28,040
Four-two.

104
00:07:28,750 --> 00:07:32,609
A week later, in Piraeus, El Kaabi twice
more.

105
00:07:32,739 --> 00:07:35,945
Two-nil. Six-two on aggregate.

106
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:40,063
Olympiacos were in a European final.

107
00:07:40,193 --> 00:07:44,320
And the final would be in Athens, at the
home of AEK.

108
00:07:46,380 --> 00:07:52,165
Twenty-ninth of May, 2024. Fiorentina,
beaten in

109
00:07:52,205 --> 00:07:55,162
the final the year before, and hungry for
it.

110
00:07:55,870 --> 00:08:01,186
The walk to the ground went through Nea
Filadelfeia, AEK's own neighbourhood.

111
00:08:01,316 --> 00:08:06,084
Red and white, on the other side of the
city, at a rival's front door.

112
00:08:06,790 --> 00:08:11,009
Twenty-six thousand, eight hundred and
forty-two inside.

113
00:08:11,710 --> 00:08:15,706
Ninety minutes. Nothing. Extra time.

114
00:08:15,836 --> 00:08:18,819
Still nothing. Penalties coming.

115
00:08:19,510 --> 00:08:22,060
The hundred and sixteenth minute.

116
00:08:22,190 --> 00:08:27,438
Santiago Hezze crosses from the left, and
Ayoub El Kaabi heads it in.

117
00:08:28,110 --> 00:08:33,100
And then the wait. A long check by the
video assistant referee.

118
00:08:33,230 --> 00:08:35,681
In the stands, nobody moved.

119
00:08:36,390 --> 00:08:41,249
The goal stood. Olympiacos one, Fiorentina
nil.

120
00:08:41,950 --> 00:08:45,158
Players on their knees on the halfway
line.

121
00:08:45,288 --> 00:08:50,858
And José Luis Mendilibar, a European
winner for the second spring running,

122
00:08:51,128 --> 00:08:53,612
with a team he had met in February.

123
00:08:54,310 --> 00:08:58,411
The first European trophy ever won by a
Greek club.

124
00:08:58,541 --> 00:09:04,281
Fifty-three years after Panathinaikos lost
to Ajax, a Greek team had won

125
00:09:04,321 --> 00:09:05,953
a European final.

126
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:12,230
That night, several thousand supporters
gathered in Piraeus.

127
00:09:12,910 --> 00:09:18,340
Thirteen days after the hundredth birthday,
the first European trophy came home

128
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:19,405
to the port.

129
00:09:20,110 --> 00:09:22,583
At home, the league was not theirs.

130
00:09:22,713 --> 00:09:26,648
Olympiacos finished third, with
seventy-four points.

131
00:09:26,778 --> 00:09:28,497
PAOK were champions.

132
00:09:29,190 --> 00:09:33,907
Ayoub El Kaabi finished with eleven goals
in the Conference League, and

133
00:09:33,947 --> 00:09:35,822
thirty-three in the season.

134
00:09:36,550 --> 00:09:41,267
And the youth team's trophy from Nyon,
five weeks earlier, beside it.

135
00:09:41,397 --> 00:09:46,764
Two European trophies in one spring, for a
country that had never won one.

136
00:09:47,470 --> 00:09:52,627
Genk, Belgrade, Freiburg, Bačka Topola,
London, Budapest, Istanbul,

137
00:09:52,667 --> 00:09:55,043
Birmingham. And Athens.

138
00:09:55,710 --> 00:09:59,659
Every supporter knows a season that ended
in nothing.

139
00:09:59,789 --> 00:10:04,095
This one went through one-four at home,
three hundred and seventy people in

140
00:10:04,135 --> 00:10:09,346
Serbia, three penalties saved in Istanbul,
and ended in the hundred and

141
00:10:09,386 --> 00:10:11,514
sixteenth minute, in Athens.

142
00:10:12,230 --> 00:10:17,788
Every match in this film is waiting in the
FanLife archive, with the games, the

143
00:10:17,828 --> 00:10:20,517
trivia and the stories of the whole club.

144
00:10:20,647 --> 00:10:24,751
Come and play it at fanlife.dubelteam.com.

145
00:10:24,881 --> 00:10:29,964
And if this story was yours too,
subscribe, and the next one will find you.
